# Frontend Architecture

## Technology Stack
- React
- TypeScript

## Structure

The frontend must be organized by responsibility, keeping pages, components, API communication, and hooks separated.

- **Pages:** Responsible for composing the interface of each application route.
- **Components:** Reusable user interface elements.
- **API:** Handles communication with the backend, including HTTP requests and response handling.
- **Hooks:** Encapsulate reusable logic and React-related functionality.

## Guidelines

- Avoid concentrating all page logic in a single component.
- Components must have clear responsibilities.
- Avoid making HTTP requests directly inside components when the logic can be encapsulated in the API layer or hooks.
- Avoid duplicating logic across pages and components.
- Maintain consistent TypeScript typing.

This rule defines only the general structure. More specific architectural decisions will be documented in separate rules as the project evolves.
